WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.939 --> 00:00:03.209
A massive protest

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.129
movement broke out in Cuba in July

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.629
of 2021.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.489
Food, medicine

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.139
and electricity shortages

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.449
exacerbated by the COVID pandemic

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.189
were pushing an already desperate,

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.409
oppressed and impoverished nation

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.359
to the brink of a rebellion.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.279
Demonstrators used the internet,

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.389
which has only been legally

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.879
available in the country since 2018,

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.709
to coordinate action in large

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.539
and small cities across the island.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.569
So the Cuban government quickly

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.699
arrested hundreds of protesters

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.229
and shut down the internet.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.209
Video of a YouTuber being pulled

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.499
out of her room in the middle of a

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.479
Spanish news broadcast went viral.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.889
Cuban President Miguel Diaz-Canel

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.809
appeared on state TV to call for

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.189
the violent suppression of the

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.329
protests against

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.710
counter-revolutionaries

00:01:10.499 --> 00:01:12.209
In Miami, members of the sizable

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.099
Cuban-American population plan to

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.749
load their own fishing boats with

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.789
supplies to make the 90 mile journey

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.619
to the island themselves,

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.029
but were deterred by the U.S.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:21.959
Coast Guard.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.279
They set off fireworks in

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.839
international waters off the coast

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.189
of Cuba instead.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.989
I think what people don't understand

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:29.909
is that the problem in Cuba stems

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.289
from the fact that people can't do

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.369
anything for themselves.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.779
How do you feed yourself?

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.849
How do you make money?

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:37.559
You're only allowed to make money if

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.569
the government says it's OK.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.489
And that's how the government

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:43.319
throttles people.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.819
They'll throw you in jail if you

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.409
decide to try and feed your family

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:46.979
on your own.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.139
Martha Bueno is a Cuban-American

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.849
activist who started the group

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.289
People for Cuba following the

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.129
protests.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.139
They assemble packages of dry foods

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.729
and medical supplies and then pay

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:58.259
people thirty five dollars a pound

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.179
to smuggle them onto the island.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:01.859
They've shipped more than 800 pounds

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.539
so far, but she says it's become

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.279
more difficult in recent months as

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.779
the Cuban government has cracked

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.459
down on smuggled supplies.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.138
The big reason that we have to

00:02:10.139 --> 00:02:11.819
smuggle it into Cuba is because if I

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.129
send it legitimately through

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.289
the Cuban government, if I raise

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.729
thousands of dollars and send a

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.919
container ship of medicine to Cuba,

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:21.929
the Cuban government will take that

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.489
and then sell it in the stores.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.409
And I wanted it to be humanitarian

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:26.969
aid people who needed it to be able

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:28.049
to receive it without paying.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.549
And I especially won't help the

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:30.629
Cuban government.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.849
I refuse to fundraise,

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.829
paid for and then give it to them

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:35.939
so that they can sell it in the

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.889
stores. I'm not that kind of girl.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.749
She certainly isn't in one of her

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:40.919
most popular tweets.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.899
Bueno, an outspoken libertarian,

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.999
wrote "When my father was 21,

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.589
he was sentenced to six years in

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:47.969
prison for attempting to leave his

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:48.929
country, Cuba.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.489
A year into his sentence, my

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.139
fearless mother broke him out of

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.339
jail.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:54.899
You might want to trade your freedom

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.699
for safety, but I sure as hell

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:57.569
don't.".

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:00.059
How did hearing these family stories

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.829
growing up affect your political

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.109
outlook and your view of current

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:05.759
day events in Cuba?

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:06.599
How can it not?

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.669
How can it not affect my political

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:11.789
views when I can contrast?

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.379
I can get on an airplane here and

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.389
leave and go anywhere, which I

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.289
do love to travel.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.999
And every time I get on an airplane,

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.979
I think about that how that

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:21.299
simple action of trying to leave

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.339
your country landed my father

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.199
with a six year sentence.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.429
I mean, everything in my life.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.229
I can draw parallel to what's

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.129
happening in Cuba.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:30.659
Cuba wasn't always that way.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.489
Political decisions

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.379
have led to people not having those

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.089
freedoms. So of course, I'm going to

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:38.039
defend the freedoms we have.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.479
I just I feel like there's no other

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:39.929
way.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:42.179
With the Cuban government, they're

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.269
they'e.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:44.129
They are.

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.130
They are not government.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:47.609
They are no government.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.859
They are a mob.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.839
Danny Lugo came to America from

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.969
Cuba 22 years ago and manages

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:56.669
logistics for Bueno's operation.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:57.929
He says that even though the

00:03:57.930 --> 00:03:59.819
communist dictatorship has survived

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.829
for 63 years, the courage

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.779
and independence of Cuba's youth

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:05.819
give him hope that change is finally

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:06.779
coming.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.729
I think there is a new generation

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:10.769
of Cubans, young Cubans

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.199
that have not been

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.599
brainwashed, so

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.609
that's how our hub.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.352
And we want to help us,

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:22.349
I mean that generation to,

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.449
you know, to to

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:25.450
win the freedom.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.499
But one Cuban citizen who spoke to

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:29.789
us anonymously for fear of

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.559
retribution from the government says

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.389
that the regime, led by President

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:35.219
Miguel Diaz-Canel, still

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:37.499
has an ironclad grip on power

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.669
and is able to quash the

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.709
demonstrations at will by cutting

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.419
off the internet and electricity.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.699
Withholding supplies and arresting

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.019
and deporting dissidents.

00:05:20.529 --> 00:05:22.479
We saw July 11, was by

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:24.459
far the most

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:26.259
important the largest, the most

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.239
widespread and

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:31.269
the most political,

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.279
openly political

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.409
of public demonstrations

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:36.429
against the region.

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:38.529
Sebastian Arcos is the associate

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:40.269
director of the Cuban Research

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.129
Institute at Florida International

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:43.479
University.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.249
His father was a political activist

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:47.409
imprisoned for years by Castro.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.089
He later died of cancer after being

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:50.679
denied treatment by the regime's

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.869
politicized health care system.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.789
Arcos points to the protests last

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:56.589
summer as a sign that the internet

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.869
is eroding the state's power.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.729
It allowed the July protests to

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.559
spread farther than has

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:04.329
ever been seen under the communist

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.849
regime, which he says is slowly

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:09.068
but surely crumbling

00:06:09.069 --> 00:06:10.179
Since the collapse of the Soviet

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:12.069
Union, the regime has been

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:14.049
slowly decomposing.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:16.599
This is a an established

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.429
process by the

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:20.949
academic literature is known as both

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:22.390
totalitarian evolution

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.829
and is an inevitable process

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:29.109
of decomposition

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:30.110
of the regime.

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.889
The regime begins to lose

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:35.779
the basic pillars, the first

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:38.449
one to go was ideology.

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:40.159
The people in the regime, they say

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:41.768
they believe it, but they drive BMWs

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:45.469
they are practicing capitalism

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:47.749
while they preach socialism

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.159
or communism to the rest of the

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:51.079
population. No one believes in them.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:53.719
Then Castro dies.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.849
The charismatic leader,

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:57.919
the man who

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:00.139
represents that

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.749
path towards paradise

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:03.619
is gone.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:04.819
Finally, they don't.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.039
They can't mobilize people anymore

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:08.959
because no one believes in what

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:10.429
they say anymore.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.229
He says that the process of reform

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:14.089
in totalitarian communist states

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:16.249
often involves cycles of opposition

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:17.359
and repression.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.309
The regime is now engaged in

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:22.069
pure naked repression.

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:23.689
What they're trying to do is trying

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:25.999
to rebuild the terror,

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.039
the state terror that Fidel Castro

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.019
successfully built in the early

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:32.419
60s that they lost.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:34.309
And people will come out into the

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:35.059
streets again.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:36.949
Meanwhile, most Cubans

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:38.119
are just looking for their next

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.709
meal. According to the source, we

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:40.710
spoke with

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.559
The Cuban government blames the dire

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:17.479
situation on the trade embargo

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:19.069
the U.S. has placed on the country.

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:20.839
Bueno says the embargo is a

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:21.499
scapegoat.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.359
It's not the embargo that

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:24.889
causes Cubans to face these

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:25.699
problems.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:26.839
It's the Cuban government that

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:28.609
causes them. Cuba's an island, and

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.529
yet people are banned

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:31.339
from fishing.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:32.899
You can't grow any food.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.279
You're not allowed to do the

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.280
simplest of things.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:59.419
The Cuban government looks to have

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:01.339
regained control after stopping

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:03.199
a second protest in November.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.089
But Bueno and Arco say the

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:06.769
status quo can't hold.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:07.909
I think things are changing.

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:08.779
You see it now.

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:10.549
You see people actually questioning

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:11.509
the Cuban government.

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:13.429
I really believe

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:15.259
that that's going

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:16.759
to lead a change that

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.799
cryptocurrencies, the ability

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.599
to go outside the government for

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:22.699
money is going to be

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:23.239
a game changer.

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:25.219
Every time they arrest a 16

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:27.409
year-old and they sentence

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:29.599
someone to 25

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:31.009
years in jail.

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:33.319
They are creating entire

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:35.959
families and neighborhoods of

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:37.819
opponents, so

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:40.039
they are feeding the opposition.

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.291
This is not Fidel Castro's

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:44.209
classic totalitarian regime

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:45.889
of the 60s and 70s.

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:47.120
It's a completely different animal.

00:09:47.121 --> 00:09:49.009
It's weak, it has

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:50.509
been wounded.

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:52.609
If Raul Castro dies

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:54.619
and is buried, we will see

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:56.389
fractures within the Communist

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:58.016
Party. Some people will refuse, to

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.789
repress the population

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:03.899
in the streets.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:06.179
That is how the Czechoslovak

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:08.159
Communist Party and the Communist

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:10.889
Party in East Germany collapse.

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:12.839
That is exactly how they

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:13.840
collapse.

